claimed: intent-no-model — implement the thing the bake-off measured toward: a classifier with NO generation on the request path, assembled rather than surveyed. Three pieces. CHAR N-GRAMS: TF-IDF over 3-5 character n-grams with a linear model, which needs no tokenizer, no embedding server and no network at all, and treats every language alike -- the direct attack on the Russian gap (0.741 against English 0.929) and the only candidate that could make the zero-network path clear 80%. STACKING: pattern votes and probe probabilities as features into one decision instead of choosing a single tier. CONFORMAL ABSTENTION: a calibrated threshold with a stated error rate, so handing the tail to a person is a guarantee rather than a hope. Then the cascade arithmetic on one split: which sequence, at which thresholds, gives the best accuracy per unit of cost, including the zero-network option. Ship the winner as a usable API with a trained model that persists, not as another table.
